# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# The Dockerfile needs exactly: pnpm-workspace.yaml, pnpm-lock.yaml,
# package.json, tsconfig.base.json, packages/, apps/${APP}/, docs/, scripts/.
# Dependencies are installed and TypeScript is compiled INSIDE the builder
# stage, so nothing here is a build input — shipping it only slows the context
# transfer and risks baking local state into an image.
#
# Two concrete problems this file prevents:
#   1. Stale build output. `tsc` does not delete orphaned files, so a
#      copied-in local dist/ would survive the in-container compile — and the
#      image could serve adapters that no longer exist in the source.
#   2. Local secrets and operator data. .env files and the SQLite databases
#      under data/ would otherwise be readable in any published image layer.

# ── Version control and CI ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.dockerignore

# ── Installed and generated ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Installed by `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` in the builder.
node_modules
**/node_modules
# Compiled in the builder; a copied-in dist would shadow it with stale files.
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.js.map

# ── Secrets and operator data ────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.scripts.example
data
**/data
# …except the admin's data-viewer templates, which are source, not data.
# `**/data` matched apps/admin/views/data/ too, so every admin image shipped
# without them and /data, /data/connections/:id and the record view all
# answered 500 (ENOENT …/views/data/index.ejs). No other tracked directory is
# named data; a new one needs its own exception here.
!apps/admin/views/data
!apps/admin/views/data/**
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
# Any depth: an anchored pattern would miss token files nested in adapter
# live-test folders, and Docker layers are additive — a later `rm -rf` cannot
# remove a file from a published layer.
**/.tokens.json
# The dev1 license-signing keypair is public on purpose (anyone may mint local dev
# licenses with it), but no build stage needs it and no image may carry it.
packages/license-token/fixtures
# Operator license files: mounted into integration-server at runtime
# (docker-compose.yml, Helm), never baked into an image.
opensteward-license
**/license.key

# ── Local operator overrides ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The image ships config.example.yml; compose mounts the real one at runtime.
docker-compose.override.yml
**/config/config.yml

# ── Development and agent tooling ────────────────────────────────────────
.claude
.superpowers
.playwright-mcp
.worktrees
tasks
CLAUDE.md
.vscode
.idea

# ── Internal notes (also excluded from git; docs-server serves docs/) ─────
docs/superpowers
docs/research

# ── Local noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.log
/swagger-*.png
/invoice-*.png
/accounting-*.png
/crm-*.png
/landing-*.png
/combined-*.png

# Platform logos are never baked into an image — see .gitignore and
# docs/operations/platform-logos.md. The `local` LOGO_SOURCE mode expects a
# volume mount at runtime, so a populated working copy must not leak in
# through `COPY docs/ docs/`.
docs/platforms/logos/
